title: Give a wiki a name
tags: Contents

A wiki's address, `ipns://k51…`, follows its newest version. A name makes it easy to say and remember.

!!! An ENS name

# Publish the wiki. The editor shows its address, `ipns://k51…`.
# Open your name in the [[ENS app|https://app.ens.domains/]].
# In ''Records'', set the ''Content Hash'' to the wiki's address, `ipns://k51…`.
# Confirm the change with your wallet.

Browsers that read ENS names, Orivon among them, then open the wiki at `yourname.eth`; other browsers reach it through gateways such as `yourname.eth.limo`. You set the Content Hash once. Every later version you publish under the same address follows it, with no new transaction.

A wiki published with ''No address'' has only the IPFS address of each version, such as `ipfs://bafy…`. Setting the Content Hash to that address shows that version until you set the next one.

!!! Subnames for a project

A project with its own name can keep its wiki under a subname, such as `wiki.yourproject.eth`, so the main name stays for the project's site.
